--- Hello World example in Tell Me a Tale ---
--  This is a comment, previous line is also a one line comment
-(  And this is a multiline comment;
    all comments will be skipped )-

-- Function definition starts with a 'this is a tale [of kind <kind>] about "<name>"'
This is a tale "Hello World". -- Note as every code block must be terminated with . or ;

 -( Function body within "so it begins" and "the end"
    Whatever strings will be ignored, if they are not keywords or keyword arguments
 -- "Say" keyword prints next arg to the terminal with a newline appended
So it begins, when I asked the storyteller to say Hello, World!.
And they actually said it. -- No keywords, this will be skipped by interpreter
The end.

 -- Function call
Tell me a tale "Hello World".
